<div id="S3.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.14</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L[C]</annotation></semantics></math> we have a cover <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b,0)\lessdot(c,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b,0)\lessdot(c,1)</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=c\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=c\in C</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in I_{L}(C)\setminus C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in I_{L}(C)\setminus C</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\not\in I_{L}(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\not\in I_{L}(C)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\lessdot c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⋖</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\lessdot c</annotation></semantics></math> is a cover in <math id="S3.Thmtheorem14.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.15</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The element <math id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,\epsilon)\in L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,\epsilon)\in L[C]</annotation></semantics></math> does not have a cover <math id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b,\alpha)\lessdot(c,\alpha^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b,\alpha)\lessdot(c,\alpha^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\neq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\neq c</annotation></semantics></math> that is a counterexample to its left modularity if and only if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in L</annotation></semantics></math> is left modular.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in L</annotation></semantics></math> is not left modular because of <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\lessdot c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⋖</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\lessdot c</annotation></semantics></math>. By <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3)</annotation></semantics></math> of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem13" title="Proposition 2.13 ([]). ‣ 2.4. Left modular lattices ‣ 2. Background ‣ Extremality in semidistributive lattices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a> this means <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\vee b=a\vee c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\vee b=a\vee c</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\wedge b=a\wedge c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\wedge b=a\wedge c</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the injection <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:L\rightarrow L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:L\rightarrow L[C]</annotation></semantics></math> following <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem14" title="Definition 2.14. ‣ 2.5. Congruence normal lattices ‣ 2. Background ‣ Extremality in semidistributive lattices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.14</span></a> and define <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b,\alpha)=\psi(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b,\alpha)=\psi(b)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c,\alpha^{\prime})=\psi(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c,\alpha^{\prime})=\psi(c)</annotation></semantics></math>, unless <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\not\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\not\in C</annotation></semantics></math>, in which case we define <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha^{\prime}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha^{\prime}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. These choices guarantee that <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b,\alpha)\lessdot(c,\alpha^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b,\alpha)\lessdot(c,\alpha^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is a cover of <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L[C]</annotation></semantics></math>. We have:</span></p>
</div>
