><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>. </span><span id="S3.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">We represent <math id="S3.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> successive doublings. The left modular elements are the blue dots. The thick red edges form the convex subsets <math id="S3.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> that we double and we circled the elements of <math id="S3.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(C)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We can now prove a characterization of the left modular elements of the doubling <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L[C]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.16</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,0)\in L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,0)\in L[C]</annotation></semantics></math> is left modular if and only if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in L</annotation></semantics></math> is left modular and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is smaller than all the maximal elements of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,1)\in L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,1)\in L[C]</annotation></semantics></math> is left modular if and only if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in L</annotation></semantics></math> is left modular and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is bigger than all the minimal elements of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,0)\lessdot(a,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,0)\lessdot(a,1)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in C</annotation></semantics></math> are two left modular elements if and only if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in L</annotation></semantics></math> is left modular and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem16.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in H(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in H(C)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma 3.15. ‣ 3.2. Extremality and left modularity of congruence normal lattices ‣ 3. The main results ‣ Extremality in semidistributive lattices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.15</span></a><span id="S3.SS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text"> tells us that the left modularity of <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,\epsilon)\in L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,\epsilon)\in L[C]</annotation></semantics></math> is seen, if <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in L</annotation></semantics></math> is left modular, by looking only at the covers of the doubling <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c,0)\lessdot(c,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c,0)\lessdot(c,1)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in C</annotation></semantics></math>. We described what happens with these covers in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem13" title="Lemma 3.13. ‣ 3.2. Extremality and left modularity of congruence normal lattices ‣ 3. The main results ‣ Extremality in semidistributive lattices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.13</span></a>. Thus by <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3)</annotation></semantics></math> of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem13" title="Proposition 2.13 ([]). ‣ 2.4. Left modular lattices ‣ 2. Background ‣ Extremality in semidistributive lattices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a> we obtain that <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,0)\in L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,0)\in L[C]</annotation></semantics></math> is left modular if and only if <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in L</annotation></semantics></math> is left modular and <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\vee c\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\vee c\in C</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in C</annotation></semantics></math>. This latter condition is equivalent to the fact that <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is smaller than all the maximal elements of <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. We deduce similarly the case of <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. The last part with <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,0)\lessdot(a,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,0)\lessdot(a,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is a direct consequence of the first part.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">Now that we understand the left modularity of the elements of <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L[C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L[C]</annotation></semantics></math>, we still need to look at the maximal left modular chains.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p">The next result is true for any lattice. A particular case gives that any maximal chain that does not intersect an interval has an element incomparable to that interval, which is not true in a general poset (see <a href="#S3.F1.sf2" title="In Figure 1 ‣ 3.1. Edge-labellings and left modularity ‣ 3. The main results ‣ Extremality in semidistributive lattices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(b)</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.17</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a convex subset of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.
Any maximal chain of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> that does not intersect <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> has an element that is neither smaller than all the maximal elements of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> nor bigger than all its minimal elements.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> be a maximal chain of <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> that does not intersect <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
The elements of this chain are split between <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> disjoint totally ordered sets : the set <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> of these that are less than all the maximal elements of <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> of these that are not less than all the maximal elements nor bigger than all the minimal elements of <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, and the set <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> of these that are bigger than all the minimal elements of <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. By convexity of <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\cap B=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\cap B=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is maximal it contains <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mn>0</mn><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mn>1</mn><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. We want to prove that <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. Seeking a contradiction, suppose that <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is partitioned between <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> which consists of the bigger elements. Since <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is maximal we have a cover relation <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\lessdot b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⋖</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\lessdot b</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in B</annotation></semantics></math>, giving us the following situation where <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> are minimal and maximal elements of <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> respectively such that <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&lt;M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&lt;M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p19.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&lt;b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.SS2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="132.84" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 124.62 132.84" width="124.62"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,132.84) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(8.27,0) translate(0,42.8)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 47.24"></path><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 70.87 70.87"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 70.87 -23.62 L 70.87 70.87"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 70.87 -23.62 L 0 47.24"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.66 -10.85)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.53em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="7.31"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 47.24"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -2.97 52.13)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="5.94"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.SS2.pic1.m2" c