<div id="S3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The following is immediate from the definition of shellability:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem29" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.29</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem29.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem29.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem29.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S3.Thmtheorem29.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1},F_{2},\dots,F_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1},F_{2},\dots,F_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a shelling of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem29.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(L)</annotation></semantics></math>, then for all <math id="S3.Thmtheorem29.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq j\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq j\leq k</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S3.Thmtheorem29.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[j-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[j-1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.Thmtheorem29.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\rightarrow F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\rightarrow F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We deduce a neccessary condition for shellability of <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> on its facet adjacency graph.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem30" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.30</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem30.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem30.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem30.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S3.Thmtheorem30.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is shellable, then <math id="S3.Thmtheorem30.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L)</annotation></semantics></math> cannot have two disjoint source sets.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume that <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L)</annotation></semantics></math> has two disjoint source sets <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. Seeking a contradiction, suppose that <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is shellable. Thus we have a shelling <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1},F_{2},\dots,F_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1},F_{2},\dots,F_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(L)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> be the left-most maximal chains of respectively <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> in our shelling. Since <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{l}\neq F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{l}\neq F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> because the source sets <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> are disjoint, without loss of generality we can assume that <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem29" title="Lemma 3.29. ‣ 3.3. Shellability of congruence normal lattices ‣ 3. The main results ‣ Extremality in semidistributive lattices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.29</span></a>, there exists <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[j-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[j-1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\rightarrow F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\rightarrow F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the left-most maximal chain of <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> in our shelling, it implies that <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\not\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\not\in T</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is a source set, this is absurd.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p">We can obtain <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L[C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L[C])</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem31" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.31</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The vertices of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L[C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L[C])</annotation></semantics></math> are the <math id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F,i)</annotation></semantics></math> for any maximal chain <math id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[|F\cap C|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[|F\cap C|]</annotation></semantics></math>. We give the edges of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L[C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L[C])</annotation></semantics></math> knowing these of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem31.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have </span><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F,i)\rightarrow(G,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F,i)\rightarrow(G,0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> whenever </span><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\rightarrow G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\rightarrow G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\cap C=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\cap C=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where </span><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[|F\cap C|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[|F\cap C|]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\cap C\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\cap C\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\cap C\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\cap C\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F,i)\rightarrow(G,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F,i)\rightarrow(G,j)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> whenever </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\rightarrow G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\rightarrow G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(F,i)\cap(G,j)|=|G|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(F,i)\cap(G,j)|=|G|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, for any </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[\,|F\,\cap C|\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.392em">∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[\,|F\,\cap C|\,]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[\,|G\,\cap C|\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.392em">∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[\,|G\,\cap C|\,]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have </span><math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F,i)\rightarrow(F,i+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F,i)\rightarrow(F,i+1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F,i+1)\rightarrow(F,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F,i+1)\rightarrow(F,i)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> whenever </span><math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|F\cap C|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|F\cap C|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, for any </span><math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[|F\cap C|-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[|F\cap C|-1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(F,0)|=|F|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(F,0)|=|F|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(F,i)|=|F|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(F,i)|=|F|+1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the result follows from <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem28" title="Lemma 3.28. ‣ 3.3. Shellability of congruence normal lattices ‣ 3. The main results ‣ Extremality in semidistributive lattices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.28</span></a> and the definition of the doubling construction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem32" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem32.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.32</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem32.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem32.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem32.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S3.Thmtheorem32.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L)</annotation></semantics></math> has at least two disjoint source sets, it is also the case for <math id="S3.Thmtheorem32.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L[C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L[C])</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> be two disjoint source sets of <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L)</annotation></semantics></math>. We define two subsets <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{C}:=\{(F,i)\mid F\in S,i\in[|F\cap C|]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{C}:=\{(F,i)\mid F\in S,i\in[|F\cap C|]\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T_{C}:=\{(G,i)\mid G\in T,i\in[|G\cap C|]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{C}:=\{(G,i)\mid G\in T,i\in[|G\cap C|]\}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L[C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L[C])</annotation></semantics></math>. We conclude by proving that the sets <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> are disjoint source sets of <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L[C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L[C])</annotation></semantics></math>. The fact that they are disjoint nonempty proper subsets of <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L[C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L[C])</annotation></semantics></math> is clear. By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem31" title="Proposition 3.31. ‣ 3.3. Shellability of congruence normal lattices ‣ 3. The main results ‣ Extremality in semidistributive lattices" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.31</span></a>, if we do not have <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\rightarrow G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\rightarrow G</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\neq G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\neq G</annotation></semantics></math>, then we do not have <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F,i)\rightarrow(G,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F,i)\rightarrow(G,j)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FA(L[C])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FA(L[C])</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows, from this observation and the fact that <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> are source sets, that <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> are source sets.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem33" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.33</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem33.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem33.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem33.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="S3.Thmtheorem33.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> does not intersect the spine of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem33.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the two sets</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S:=\{(F,i)\mid F\in FA(L),\,F\cap C\neq\emptyset,\,i\in[|F\cap C|]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\{(F,i)\mid F\in FA(L),\,F\cap C\neq\emptyset,\,i\in[|F\cap C|]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem33.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem33.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T:=\{(G,0)\mid G\text{ is a longest chain of }L\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> is a longest chain of </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T:=\{(G,0)\mid G\text{ is a longest chain of }L\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
